-- title:
--   Sect. 4d, proof of the converse — Bayes rationality in the system generated by f restates (2.2)
-- statement:
--   Let $f:\Gamma\to S$ be a correlated strategy $n$-tuple on a finite probability space $(\Gamma,q)$ for a game with payoffs $h$. Take $\Omega:=\Gamma$, prior $p:=q$, action $n$-tuple $\mathbf s:=f$, and let $\mathcal P^i$ be the partition of $\Gamma$ generated by $f^i$, so that $\gamma$ and $\gamma'$ lie in the same element of $\mathcal P^i$ iff $f^i(\gamma)=f^i(\gamma')$. Then
--   $$
--   \text{every player is Bayes rational at every }\gamma\in\Gamma\iff f\text{ is a correlated equilibrium.}
--   $$
--
--   This is the observation behind the converse of the Main Theorem: in the information system generated by $f$, Bayesian rationality is a restatement of condition (2.2).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $q$ is a probability vector but need not have full support; Bayes rationality at states of null cells is vacuous.
-- source:
--   Aumann, Correlated Equilibrium as an Expression of Bayesian Rationality, Econometrica 55 (1987), DOI 10.2307/1911154, p. 11 (PDF p. 12), Sect. 4d

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_agt_games
import Definitions.Def_Aumann1987_BayesRational_CorrelatedEquilibrium
import Definitions.Def_Aumann1987_BayesRational_InformationSystem

namespace Aumann1987.BayesRational

/-- **Sect. 4d, proof of the converse — Bayesian rationality restates (2.2)** (Aumann 1987,
Econometrica 55, Sect. 4d, p. 11, PDF p. 12): "We need only define `(Ω, p) := Γ`, `s := f`, and
`𝒫ⁱ` to be the partition of `Ω` generated by `fⁱ` (i.e., `ω` and `ω′` are in the same element
of `𝒫ⁱ` iff `fⁱ(ω) = fⁱ(ω′)`). Bayesian rationality is then a restatement of (2.2)."

Let `f : Γ → S` be a correlated strategy `n`-tuple on a finite probability space `(Γ, q)`, and
let `𝒫ⁱ` be the partition of `Γ` generated by `fⁱ`. Then every player is Bayes rational at every
state of `Γ` (with prior `q`, partitions `𝒫ⁱ`, and action `n`-tuple `f`) if and only if `f` is
a correlated equilibrium.

**Formalization Note.** The partition generated by `fⁱ` is `Setoid.ker (fun γ => f γ i)`, whose
relation is `fⁱ(γ) = fⁱ(γ')`. `q` is a probability vector (`AGT.IsLottery`) but need not have
full support; at states whose cell is null, Bayes rationality is vacuous (see `condExp`). -/
theorem bayes_rational_iff_ce {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {S : ι → Type*}
    {Γ : Type*} [Fintype Γ] (h : ι → (∀ i, S i) → ℝ) (q : Γ → ℝ) (hq : AGT.IsLottery q)
    (f : Γ → ∀ i, S i) :
    (∀ (i : ι) (γ : Γ),
        IsBayesRationalAt h q (fun j => Setoid.ker (fun γ' => f γ' j)) f i γ) ↔
      IsCorrelatedEquilibrium h q f := by sorry

end Aumann1987.BayesRational
